    "pros": [
      "Lowest cost per 25 g of protein in the Levels range",
      "Same 24 g scoop and monk fruit formula",
      "71 servings per tub, per the listing"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "A lot of powder to get through if you dislike the flavor",
      "Same certification gap as the smaller tub"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The tub to reorder, not the one to start with.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein per serving": "24 g (label)",
      "Calories": "About 130 (databases)",
      "Third-party testing": "No certification found",
      "Best for": "Regular Levels buyers"
    },
    "amazonUrl": "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B072M8FKRW"
  },
  {
    "id": "levels-micellar-casein",
    "name": "Levels 100% Micellar Casein (Chocolate, 2 lb)",
    "brand": "Levels",
    "badge": "Best Before Bed",
    "category": "Micellar casein protein",
    "description": "Levels' casein lists 24 g of protein and 5.2 g of BCAAs per scoop with no added sugar, per the listing, from hormone-free dairy. The chocolate flavor uses cacao powder and natural flavor and is sweetened with monk fruit. Micellar casein digests slowly, which makes it a common before-bed shake. Buyer feedback on texture is more mixed than for the whey.",
    "pros": [
      "24 g of slow-digesting protein per scoop, per the label",
